    "mermaidDiagram": "## Flow Diagram (Mermaid)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Render React counter component] --> B[useState initializes count to 0]\n    B --> C[UI displays counter value]\n    C --> D[User clicks increment/update button]\n    D --> E[onClick handler runs]\n    E --> F[setCount is called]\n\n    F --> G{What happens next?}\n\n    G --> H[JSX is not rendering count state]\n    H --> I[UI still shows hardcoded/stale 0]\n\n    G --> J[setCount uses wrong value]\n    J --> K[State stays 0 or unchanged]\n\n    G --> L[Component remounts after click]\n    L --> M[State resets to useState 0]\n\n    G --> N[Effect/parent logic overrides state]\n    N --> O[Count briefly changes then returns to 0]\n\n    G --> P[Click wiring/form behavior is wrong]\n    P --> Q[Intended update does not persist]\n\n    I --> R[Observed bug: counter display remains 0]\n    K --> R\n    M --> R\n    O --> R\n    Q --> R\n```\n\n## Clarifying Questions\n\n1. Does the JSX that displays the counter render `{count}` directly, or is it showing a prop, constant, ref, or hardcoded `0`?\n2. What is the exact `onClick` handler code, including the value passed to `setCount`?\n3. When you add `console.log(count)` in the component body, does the logged value ever change after clicking?\n4. Is the counter component inside a parent that changes its `key`, conditionally renders it, or otherwise remounts it on click?\n5. Is the button inside a `<form>` or is there any `useEffect` / prop-sync logic that could reset `count` back to `0`?\n\n## Confidence Score\n\nCONFIDENCE_SCORE: 80",
