    "mermaidDiagram": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Route/page loads] --> B[Parent component renders]\n    B --> C[ProductList mount begins]\n    C --> D[ProductList evaluates value used at ProductList.jsx:24]\n    D --> E{Is mapped value a defined array?}\n\n    E -->|Yes| F[Call array.map successfully]\n    F --> G[ProductList renders UI]\n    G --> H[React mount completes]\n\n    E -->|No: undefined| I[ProductList calls undefined.map]\n    I --> J[TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined<br/>reading 'map']\n    J --> K[Render crashes and ProductList fails to mount]\n\n    classDef happy fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#16a34a,color:#166534;\n    classDef bug fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b;\n    classDef diverge fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,color:#92400e;\n\n    class A,B,C,D,F,G,H happy;\n    class E diverge;\n    class I,J,K bug;\n```",
    "clarifyingQuestions": "1. What is the exact expression on `ProductList.jsx:24` that calls `.map(...)`, and what is the variable name being mapped?\n2. On the first render, does that variable come from props, local state, a selector, context, or a derived helper/memoized value?\n3. In the parent component, is `ProductList` ever rendered without the expected list prop, or with `products={undefined}` during initial load?\n4. If the data is async, how is the relevant list initialized before the fetch/query completes: `useState([])`, `useState()`, or equivalent store/query default?\n5. Does the runtime payload/store snapshot match the shape `ProductList` expects at render time, e.g. `products` versus `items` or another nested path?",
