    "mermaidDiagram": "## 1. Flow Diagram (Mermaid)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Latest deployment reaches production] --> B[User submits POST /api/auth/login]\n    B --> C[Login handler starts auth flow]\n    C --> D{Auth dependencies/config/code path healthy?}\n\n    D -->|Yes| E[Load config/secrets and initialize auth components]\n    E --> F[Lookup user / validate credentials]\n    F --> G[Generate session/JWT and return success]\n    G --> H[User logs in successfully]\n\n    D -->|No - post-deploy regression| I[Broken config/secret OR DB failure OR code exception]\n    I --> J[Unhandled server-side exception in login path]\n    J --> K[API returns HTTP 500]\n    K --> L[All login attempts fail; production auth outage]\n\n    style E fill:#d4edda,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n    style F fill:#d4edda,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n    style G fill:#d4edda,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n    style H fill:#d4edda,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n\n    style D fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#f57f17,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n    style I fill:#ffe0b2,stroke:#ef6c00,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n\n    style K fill:#f8d7da,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n    style L fill:#f8d7da,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px,color:#000\n```\n\n## 2. Clarifying Questions\n\n1. What is the exact exception/stack trace in production logs for a failed `/api/auth/login` request immediately after the latest deployment?\n2. Did the latest deployment change any auth-related environment variables, secrets, or secret names/paths such as `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `SESSION_SECRET`, or IdP configuration?\n3. Do other production endpoints that use the same database connection succeed, or are there concurrent DB connection/authentication/schema errors across the service?\n4. Was any code, middleware, dependency, or migration affecting login/authentication included in the last release, and if so, which files/packages changed?\n5. If you roll back to the previous production build without changing data, does `/api/auth/login` immediately recover from HTTP 500 to normal behavior?\n\n## 3. Confidence Score & Breakdown\n\nCONFIDENCE_SCORE: 92\nCONFIDENCE_EVIDENCE: [\"The failure began immediately after the latest deployment, strongly indicating a deployment-induced regression\", \"The issue affects all users and reproduces on every login request, which fits a global config/dependency/code-path failure\", \"The endpoint returns HTTP 500 rather than an auth error, indicating a server-side exception in the login path\"]\nCONFIDENCE_ASSUMPTIONS: [\"The reported timing relative to deployment is accurate and not coincidental\", \"The login path depends on shared configuration, database access, or common auth middleware used on every request\"]\nCONFIDENCE_MISSING: [\"Exact production stack trace or error log for `/api/auth/login`\", \"Deployment diff covering code changes, env var changes, secret rotation, and any auth-related migrations\"]\n\n## 4. Severity Classification\n\nSEVERITY: critical\nSEVERITY_REASON: This is a production outage on the core authentication path with 100% reproducibility affecting all users and preventing access to the system.",
