    "mermaidDiagram": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Two users load same record] --> B[Both receive same initial state/version]\n    B --> C[User A edits record]\n    B --> D[User B edits record]\n    C --> E[User A submits update]\n    D --> F[User B submits update]\n\n    E --> G{Does update path enforce concurrency check<br/>version/ETag/If-Match/row lock?}\n    F --> G\n\n    G -->|Yes| H[First update succeeds]\n    H --> I[Second update detected as stale]\n    I --> J[Return conflict response<br/>409/412 or merge/retry flow]\n    J --> K[User notified; no silent overwrite]\n\n    G -->|No / bypassed| L[Both updates accepted by ID only]\n    L --> M[Later write overwrites earlier write]\n    M --> N[Both requests appear successful]\n    N --> O[One user's changes are silently lost]\n\n    style A fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style B fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style C fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style D fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style E fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style F fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style H fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style I fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style J fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n    style K fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32\n\n    style G fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ef6c00\n    style L fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828\n    style M fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828\n    style N fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828\n    style O fill:#ffcdd2,stroke:#b71c1c\n```",
    "clarifyingQuestions": "1. Does the record schema and update API include any concurrency token such as a `version`, `updated_at`, revision number, `ETag`, or `If-Match` header, and is that value present in the actual request payload/headers during reproduction?\n2. What exact SQL/ORM operation is used by this failing update path: does it update by primary key only, or does it include a predicate like `WHERE id = ? AND version = ?`?\n3. Is this issue reproducible across all edit flows for the same entity, or only in one specific endpoint/UI path such as inline edit, PATCH, admin edit, or bulk/custom save?\n4. When two users edit different fields on the same record and save concurrently, does one user’s unrelated field change also disappear, indicating a stale full-record overwrite rather than field-level merge/patch behavior?\n5. In server logs during a reproduction, do you see any optimistic-lock/conflict exceptions or retry middleware activity that would indicate detection is happening but being swallowed before reaching the user?",
