    "mermaidDiagram": "## 1. Flow Diagram (Mermaid)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[User logs into app in Firefox] --> B[User lands on protected route]\n    B --> C[User remains idle for 30 minutes]\n    C --> D[Session expires on server/client auth state]\n    D --> E[Next authenticated action or auth check occurs]\n\n    E --> F[App detects expired session]\n    F --> G[Clear auth/session state]\n    G --> H[Redirect to /login]\n    H --> I[Login page displayed]\n\n    E --> J[Bug divergence: Firefox expired-session handling misbehaves]\n    J --> K[JS error OR inconsistent auth state OR missed idle/focus redirect callback]\n    K --> L[Router/guard fails to navigate or renders nothing]\n    L --> M[Blank page shown instead of login]\n\n    style A fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style B fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style C fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style D fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style E fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style F fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style G fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style H fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style I fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n\n    style J fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ef6c00,stroke-width:2px\n    style K fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style L fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style M fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n```\n\n## 2. Clarifying Questions\n\n1. In Firefox DevTools Console at the exact moment the blank page appears, do you see any uncaught exception, unhandled promise rejection, or router/render error, and what is the full stack trace?\n2. For the first network request made after the 30-minute idle period, what exact response does Firefox receive compared with Chrome: status code, response headers, content type, and body shape?\n3. Immediately before and after expiry in Firefox, what are the values of the auth cookie, localStorage token keys, and sessionStorage auth markers, and do they differ from the same state transition in Chrome?\n4. Does the URL change to the login route when the blank page appears, or does it remain on the protected route while rendering nothing?\n5. Is the issue reproducible only when the tab is backgrounded/minimized during the idle period, or also when Firefox stays foregrounded and focused for the full timeout?\n\n## 3. Confidence Score & Breakdown\n\nCONFIDENCE_SCORE: 82\nCONFIDENCE_EVIDENCE: [\"The blank page symptom strongly suggests a frontend crash or render-null state during session-expiration handling.\", \"The issue is explicitly Firefox-specific, which aligns with browser-specific storage, timer, or navigation behavior differences.\", \"The trigger is tightly scoped to idle timeout expiration, narrowing likely causes to auth expiry, interceptors, guards, and redirect flow.\"]\nCONFIDENCE_ASSUMPTIONS: [\"The application is a SPA using client-side routing and frontend-managed auth/session state.\", \"The blank page is caused by client-side behavior rather than a server-rendered empty response.\"]\nCONFIDENCE_MISSING: [\"No Firefox console errors or stack traces were provided.\", \"No network trace or auth storage/cookie state comparison across browsers was provided.\"]\n\n## 4. Severity Classification\n\nSEVERITY: high\nSEVERITY_REASON: This blocks users from recovering normally after session expiration in a core authentication flow, is reproducible under a common idle-timeout scenario, and causes loss of app usability even though no direct data corruption risk is yet evident.",
