    "mermaidDiagram": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[User logs into app in Safari] --> B[User lands on protected/authenticated page]\n    B --> C[User becomes inactive for idle/session timeout period]\n    C --> D[App/session expiry handling begins<br/>idle timer, session check, token refresh, or route guard]\n\n    D --> E{Auth expiry flow handled cleanly?}\n\n    E -->|Yes| F[Session recognized as expired]\n    F --> G[Redirect user to login page]\n    G --> H[User sees login screen]\n\n    E -->|No - Safari-specific divergence| I[Safari-specific auth/state failure<br/>cookie not sent, refresh fails, timer delayed, storage missing, or JS exception]\n    I --> J[Auth state becomes null/invalid or unresolved]\n    J --> K{Redirect/error handling executes?}\n    K -->|No| L[Protected route/layout renders nothing or app crashes]\n    L --> M[White/blank screen shown]\n    K -->|Partially / race condition| L\n\n    style A fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style B fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style C fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style D fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style E fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ef6c00,stroke-width:2px\n    style F fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style G fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style H fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px\n    style I fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style J fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style K fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style L fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px\n    style M fill:#ffCDD2,stroke:#b71c1c,stroke-width:3px\n```",
    "clarifyingQuestions": "1. In Safari Web Inspector, what is the first auth-related network response after returning from inactivity: does `/me`, session-check, refresh, or logout return `401/403`, fail entirely, or succeed?\n2. Does the Safari Console show any uncaught JavaScript error or promise rejection at the exact moment the screen turns white, and if so, what is the stack trace and source file?\n3. Does the bug reproduce only when the Safari tab is backgrounded or the device sleeps, or also when the tab stays foregrounded and visible for the full idle timeout?\n4. After the blank screen appears, are the auth cookies and any auth-related localStorage/sessionStorage values still present in Safari, and are those cookies being sent on the next request?\n5. If you manually navigate to the login route or refresh the page after the blank screen, does the app recover cleanly to login, or does it remain broken/blank until storage/cookies are cleared?",
