    "mermaidDiagram": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[User opens app / enters affected flow] --> B[Vendor/framework code dispatches lifecycle/event]\n    B --> C[Application code in main.abc123.js anonymous function runs]\n    C --> D{Value bound to minified identifier 'a' is callable?}\n\n    D -->|Yes| E[Invoke a()]:::happy\n    E --> F[Handler/import/state function executes normally]:::happy\n    F --> G[User flow completes without runtime error]:::happy\n\n    D -->|No| H[Application still attempts a()]:::bug\n    H --> I[TypeError: a is not a function]:::fail\n    I --> J[JS execution aborts at main.abc123.js:1:4521]:::fail\n    J --> K[Affected UI flow breaks / current action fails]:::fail\n\n    classDef happy fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#16a34a,color:#166534;\n    classDef bug fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,color:#92400e;\n    classDef fail fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b;\n```",
    "clarifyingQuestions": "1. Can you provide the source-mapped original file/function for `main.abc123.js:1:4521`, and specifically whether `a` resolves to a prop/argument, imported symbol, or local state variable?\n2. Immediately before the failing call, what are the runtime values of `typeof a`, `a`, and any surrounding arguments/props in the paused DevTools frame?\n3. Does the error reproduce only on specific UI states such as empty data, partial async load, post-navigation remount, or feature-flagged variants, or does it happen deterministically on every attempt?\n4. Were there any recent changes to imports/exports, dependency versions, bundler/transpiler config, or CommonJS/ESM interop around the component or module mapped from this call site?\n5. Under network throttling or delayed initialization, does the failure become more frequent, indicating that `a` is expected to be assigned later but is being invoked too early?",
